# The policy set, owned by the repository owner (decision 0008, #680).
#
# GitHub reads this file for two things. Always: it auto-requests the owner's
# review on a pull request touching a path below. Only once `main-protect`
# carries a `pull_request` rule with `require_code_owner_review`: such a pull
# request cannot merge without the owner's approval on GitHub. Until that rule
# exists this file claims nothing, which is why it may merge before the rule --
# and why the rule must NOT be added before the seats author as an identity
# other than the owner: GitHub does not count an author's approval of their own
# pull request. The order is in docs/decisions/0008 and is 0005's.
#
# Nothing in the test gate opens this file (tests/closure.py lists it INERT).

/CLAUDE.md                     @tvofi
/.claude/rules/                @tvofi
/.cursor/rules/                @tvofi
/tools/audit/briefs/           @tvofi
# COMMON.md is the finder's contract and is not policy (CLAUDE.md says so);
# a line with a path and no owner un-owns it.
/tools/audit/briefs/COMMON.md
/docs/decisions/               @tvofi
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @tvofi
